      en: "Brīvkalni Hill is situated in the central part of the Vidzeme Highland, one of the highest regions in Latvia. This elevation is part of a complex system of terminal moraines formed during the last Ice Age by the pressure of massive glacial lobes. Standing over 190 meters high, the hill offers expansive views of the undulating surroundings, characterized by deep valleys and small lakes. Geologically, Brīvkalni consists primarily of gravel and sand deposits typical of glacial accumulation forms. Historically, the Vidzeme region was known for its fortified settlements, with surrounding ridges often serving as strategic points. Today, Brīvkalni is a vital component of the local ecosystem, hosting rare plant species adapted to the cooler highland climate. The area around the hill is utilized for hiking in the summer and skiing in the winter, making it a significant recreational destination. Scientific monitoring of erosion processes on its slopes provides important data for soil conservation efforts in Latvia.",
